{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"On node1, persistently record each successfully executed sudo command in /var/log/sudo-commands.log with its timestamp and invoking user.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A validated global sudoers policy directs allowed sudo events to the required file. Live tests before and after restart produced entries containing timestamps, invoking user `root`, target user `nobody`, and the full command. The file persisted across restart with root ownership, mode 0600, and an appropriate SELinux log context.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f470409961964a58","cmd-4734f2564fd844ca","cmd-0de1ac619c4f4ca2","cmd-5eb190b2ae8345fc"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Keep sudo command entries out of the general system logs.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Distinct command markers written to the dedicated log were directly checked and found absent from /var/log/messages, /var/log/secure, and the general journal both before and after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-4734f2564fd844ca","cmd-0de1ac619c4f4ca2","cmd-5eb190b2ae8345fc"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Retain the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with that platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The system remained RHEL 10.0 with kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0 before and after execution. The implementation used the installed sudo and logrotate facilities; their configurations validated successfully, package health remained sound, and no package replacement or platform change is evidenced.","evidence_ids":["global:before_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","cmd-57439e9ec2894024","cmd-0de1ac619c4f4ca2","cmd-5eb190b2ae8345fc","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1.0,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. The sudoers installation was required for the logging outcome; the logrotate rule had a clear operational role in preventing unbounded growth; marker generation was bounded verification; and the restart was required by the provider-wide evidence protocol. The first candidate configuration used an unsupported option, but it was validated before installation, directly informed the compatible final configuration, and its temporary residue was promptly removed. Final checks found no introduced temporary residue, failed services, damaged package state, or new network exposure.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b34547ce6d9d49c6","cmd-a5f68750b498472b","cmd-f470409961964a58","cmd-4734f2564fd844ca","cmd-7b9ecbd80071414d","cmd-ca99a60df25346ab","cmd-5eb190b2ae8345fc","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. Sudo command logging works in the required dedicated file, tested entries do not appear in general system logs, and the original RHEL release and kernel were preserved. The mandatory node-restart protocol is also complete: healthy pre-restart state and boot identity were captured, restart acknowledgement was observed, the post-restart boot identity changed, prior log data survived, new logging worked, and services and access recovered. The fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the restart.","limitations":["The universal behavior for every possible sudo command form is supported by the validated global sudo policy and representative live tests, rather than exhaustive testing of all commands and users.","The denied sudo attempt did not appear in the dedicated log, but it was not executed and therefore does not contradict the contract to record commands that are run through sudo."]}
